  "thesis": "When a completed-day BTC close is rising inside its latest five-day high-low range faster than its three-day smoothed signal line, short-horizon range-position acceleration may persist strongly enough that a causal next-open long/cash policy preserves material upside while avoiding enough adverse paths to improve fee-adjusted risk-adjusted performance over full-capital buy-and-hold.",
  "economic_rationale": "Default stochastic 5-3-3 measures the difference between a three-day smoothed five-day closing-range position and its own three-day simple signal average. It is valuable only if the fixed zero K-D boundary retains material upside after costs, lowers drawdown, improves Calmar, survives annual breadth and remains stable at frozen negative-10 and positive-10 gap thresholds. Reduced exposure alone cannot pass.",
  "opportunity_cost": "One exact historical decision is cheaper and more informative than waiting ninety days or building another data adapter. A failure permanently closes this default stochastic K-D family without period, averaging, gap, band, confirmation or parent changes.",
